=== SURVEY ===
Web source BackgroundWorkSegment.tsx is a footer status-bar segment over `useBackgroundJobs()` →
`{ jobs, count, hasJobs }` (jobs sorted oldest-first by startedAt). It returns `null` when `!hasJobs`
(hidden while quiet). When work is in flight it renders a `<Tooltip>`-wrapped `<button>`: a spinning
Loader2 + (unless `iconOnly`) the summary text — `count === 1 ? t('statusBar.background.one','1 task')
: t('statusBar.background.many','{{count}} tasks',{count})` — tinted amber, with
aria-label `${t('statusBar.background.aria','Background tasks')}: ${summary}` and tooltip
`${t('statusBar.background.tooltip','Background work in progress')} · ${summary}`. Tapping toggles a
`role="dialog"` popover (heading `t('statusBar.background.heading','Running')`) listing each job: a
per-kind glyph (KIND_ICON: export→FileDown, mutation→Save, custom→Sparkles), the job label + optional
description, and a trailing spinner. Click-outside / Escape close it; a `useEffect` closes it when
`!hasJobs`. useBackgroundJobs aggregates active export jobs (queued/processing → label
`file_name || '{type} export'`, desc 'Queued'/'Processing'), a composite mutation job
('Saving…' / 'Saving {n} changes…') from useIsMutating(), and module-scoped registerJob custom jobs.
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation, useBackgroundJobs. Shared components: @/components/ui (Tooltip).
Charts/maps: none. Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/VersionSegment (0181) — the
sibling footer status-bar segment (Adapter/Model/Seams/Polling/View/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests).

=== REASONING ===
- The native surface reproduces the web composition as a status-bar segment bound through
  `BackgroundWorkSegmentModel` (no HTTP/aggregation in the view): the active state is the spinner +
  summary button opening a native `.popover` running-jobs list; the orthogonal connection axis is a
  freshness chip inside the popover.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical VersionSegment leaf:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): BackgroundWorkSurface (slug + 5s web poll cadence), BackgroundWorkConnection,
    BackgroundJobKind (+ SF-Symbol peers of KIND_ICON + VoiceOver names), BackgroundJob (web BackgroundJob),
    BackgroundWorkSnapshot, BackgroundWorkData, BackgroundWorkResolved + BackgroundWorkProjection (the
    web hasJobs/count/oldest-first-sort derivation + the P4 leaf precedence error→loading→empty),
    BackgroundWorkSummary (web `count===1?one:many`), BackgroundWorkAccessibility (tooltip + aria builders).
  • Model: BackgroundWorkTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; BackgroundWorkStrings
    i18n facade (P1/S10); @Observable BackgroundWorkSegmentModel — popover open state (web useState(open))
    with the open-only-when-active guard + the close-on-drain rule (web useEffect on hasJobs), one-shot
    stale auto-refresh, hasJobs (web hasJobs gate so a host can hide while quiet).
  • Seams: BackgroundWorkSource protocol (+InMemory); MutationActivityObserver (web useIsMutating, +InMemory);
    BackgroundCustomJobObserver + BackgroundCustomJobRegistry (web module-scoped registerJob: idempotent by
    id, returns a cleanup closure, process-wide .shared); BackgroundWorkPoller (web pollWhileActive, +Manual);
    BackgroundWorkTimestamp.
  • Polling: BackgroundExportStatus/BackgroundExportJob + ExportJobsProbe (+Closure/+Scripted) — web
    useExportJobs; TimerBackgroundWorkPoller; PollingBackgroundWorkSource — aggregates the three signals
    into one job list exactly like the web hook (active-export filter + map, composite mutation job, custom
    rows), drives the freshness axis off the export probe.
  • View (swift) + Views + States + Previews + strings + AdapterTests/ModelTests/PollingTests.
- The web `if (!hasJobs) return null` (hidden while quiet) is reproduced AND surfaced as the P4 `empty`
  leaf: a friendly "No background work" pill (never a blank box), with `model.hasJobs` exposed so a host
  may instead hide the surface to match the web's literal quietness. This is the predecessor-accepted
  disposition for a web component that folds a state away (sibling VersionSegment surfaces the probe
  lifecycle its web hook hides). loading/error leaves surface the /export/jobs probe lifecycle the web
  hook swallows.
- Native idioms (not Tailwind ports): the click-outside / Escape dismissal is the native `.popover`
  behaviour (no manual mousedown/keydown listeners); the Loader2 spinner is the system `ProgressView`;
  amber is Color.TS.statusWarning; the popover/chip/pills use the P1/S9 tokens. The mutation job's
  startedAt is set once on the 0→positive transition (stable sort) rather than the web's per-render
  `new Date()`.

